__baseline__.text:
useEffect double-fire cause: React 18 Strict Mode, dev only. Mount → unmount → remount, checks effect cleanup correct.

Fix: not a bug. Don't suppress with refs/flags — write proper cleanup instead:

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const controller = new AbortController();
  fetchData(controller.signal);
  return () => controller.abort();
}, []);
```

Prod build: runs once. Only StrictMode + dev trigger double-run, catches missing cleanup early.

__terse__.text:
Default React behavior: parent re-render → all children re-render, unless opted out.

Causes:
- No `React.memo` wrap → child re-renders regardless of prop change.
- Inline props (`{}`, `[]`, arrow fns) → new ref each render → breaks memo even if wrapped.
- Context consumer → re-renders on any context value change, even unrelated fields.

Fix:
```jsx
const Child = React.memo(function Child({ data, onClick }) {
  ...
});

// parent
const data = useMemo(() => ({...}), [deps]);
const onClick = useCallback(() => {...}, [deps]);
```

Other options: move state closer to where used (avoid lifting unnecessarily), split context by concern, pass `children` as prop (children don't re-render if parent's own state changes but children ref unchanged).

Check with React DevTools Profiler → highlight "why did this render" to confirm cause before fixing.

StrictMode cause. Dev-only: mount → unmount → mount, simulate future double-mount behavior, surface unsafe side effects.

Why: catch effects missing cleanup (subscriptions, timers, listeners) that break on remount.

Fix: don't disable StrictMode. Write cleanup fn:

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const sub = subscribe();
  return () => sub.unsubscribe(); // cleanup
}, []);
```

Prod build: no double-invoke, runs once. Effect idempotent + cleaned up → double-run harmless.

hmd_lite.text:
Dev mode → `React.StrictMode` intentionally double-invokes render + effects (mount → unmount → mount) to surface unsafe side effects.

Reason: helps catch bugs where effect lacks proper cleanup (subscriptions, timers, listeners not removed) — bugs that'd bite later w/ concurrent features.

Prod build: runs once. No StrictMode: runs once.

Fix (if effect breaks on double-run): add cleanup function.

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const sub = subscribe();
  return () => sub.unsubscribe(); // cleanup — fixes double-run issue
}, []);
```

Don't remove StrictMode to "fix" — masks real bug instead of fixing it.

hmd_full.text:
StrictMode double-invoke, dev only. Mount→unmount→remount, catch missing cleanup.

Cause: React 18 StrictMode simulate mount/unmount/remount for effects. Expose bugs where cleanup missing.

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const sub = subscribe();
  return () => sub.unsubscribe(); // missing this = broken app in prod too, StrictMode just surfaces it early
}, []);
```

Prod build: no double-run. Fix: always return cleanup fn matching setup. Don't suppress via disabling StrictMode — masks real bugs.

hmd_ultra.text:
StrictMode (dev only) → mount, unmount, remount deliberately. Surfaces effects without cleanup (leaks, stale subs, double listeners).

Fix: return cleanup fn matching effect.

```js
useEffect(() => {
  const id = setInterval(tick, 1000);
  return () => clearInterval(id);
}, []);
```

Prod build: runs once. Not a bug — StrictMode expose fragile effects early.
